  -F "data={\"slug\":\"apartment-vs-house-nepal\",\"title\":\"Apartment vs House in Nepal: Which is Right for You?\",\"category\":\"Comparison\",\"excerpt\":\"Should you buy an apartment or a house in Nepal? We compare both options across cost, maintenance, lifestyle, and investment potential to help you make the right choice.\",\"content\":\"Choosing between an apartment and a house depends on your lifestyle, budget, and long-term plans. Apartments offer: lower maintenance costs, shared amenities like gyms and security, prime locations in urban areas, and easier resale. Houses offer: more space and privacy, customization freedom, land ownership, and potential for expansion. Cost comparison: Apartments in Kathmandu range from 15 lakh to 1 crore NPR while houses start from 25 lakh and go up significantly. Maintenance: Apartments have monthly maintenance fees but less individual upkeep. Houses require full responsibility for maintenance but offer complete control. Investment: Both appreciate well but apartments in prime locations often have better rental yields. Consider your family size, daily commute, and future plans when deciding.\",\"author\":\"Priya Maharjan\",\"authorRole\":\"Customer Relations Lead\",\"readTime\":\"7 min read\",\"isFeatured\":false}"
